OpenWings patch 0021: Connect (use what you already have, in one click)

Setting up an AI and apps meant URLs, keys and forms. This patch adds one
click choices that use what people already have, and switches off the
upstream sign-ins that pose as another company's app.

  * static/js/wings-connect.js (new), static/index.html: "Connect your
    AI" in the empty #welcome-setup container while no model endpoint
    exists, and as a card in Settings > Add Models: models already on
    this computer (/api/discover, one click to add; a one line Ollama
    hint when none is found), Connect OpenRouter (its OAuth PKCE flow,
    wings/connect_routes.py), Paste a key (provider picker with each
    provider's own key page, prefix detection, Test), and a plain panel
    for Claude, ChatGPT and Gemini subscribers. "Connect your apps" in
    Settings > Integrations: Notion, Linear, Jira and Confluence through
    the existing MCP OAuth client, with Connected / Reconnect /
    Disconnect.
  * app.py: mounts wings/connect_routes.py next to the MCP routes.
  * src/mcp_oauth.py, routes/mcp/mcp_routes.py: a sign-in returns to the
    origin the browser uses when it is trusted (wings/origin.py), not a
    fixed localhost:7000; the callback completes only for the person who
    started the flow, and only from a signed-in person's own browser (an
    admin's for flows started by the app, an API token or the agent);
    Google MCP sign-ins get a random state bound to that person, a ten
    minute expiry and S256 PKCE (wings/mcp_google.py) instead of the
    server id; Cancel on the app's own page ends the waiting sign-in at
    once; the client registers as "OpenWings"; result pages are in
    OpenWings' own plain style; the server list says whether an app was
    ever signed in (no token data).
  * src/mcp_manager.py: when discovery or sign-in fails inside the MCP
    SDK's transport, the connect is reported as an error ("Could not reach
    the server's sign-in service", "The sign-in did not finish") instead of
    re-raising the SDK's cancellation into the web request (a bare HTTP 500)
    or leaving a stale "waiting for sign-in".
  * src/chatgpt_subscription.py, src/copilot.py, routes/copilot_routes.py,
    routes/chatgpt_subscription_routes.py, src/llm_core.py,
    src/endpoint_resolver.py, static/js/admin.js, static/js/slashCommands.js:
    ChatGPT Subscription (OpenAI's Codex app id), GitHub Copilot (VS
    Code's app id) and Kimi Code's borrowed User-Agent are off unless the
    deployment sets WINGS_ALLOW_UNOFFICIAL_SIGNIN=1 (wings/unofficial.py).
    Off: not offered in Settings or /setup (which explains why), existing
    connections keep their data and every call answers with a plain note
    on why and how to turn it back on at the owner's own risk. Nothing at
    all goes to those services while off: model lists, probes, pings and
    background refreshes (routes/model_routes.py), the agent's model
    lookup (src/ai_interaction.py, src/agent_tools/
    model_interaction_tools.py) and webhooks (routes/webhook/
    webhook_routes.py) skip them, their stored token reaches no caller,
    no borrowed headers are built, and new endpoints or tests for them
    are refused.
  * static/js/settings.js, routes/email/email_helpers.py: Gmail, iCloud
    and Yahoo presets show short steps and a link to the provider's app
    password page; the Outlook preset says Outlook sign-in is coming and
    what to do for now, and hides the account fields, instead of failing
    after Create. static/js/settings.js, static/js/emailLibrary/
    settingsPage.js: visible "Odysseus" wording says OpenWings.
  * scripts/generate_env_reference.py, website/configuration-reference.md:
    the Copilot client id note names the new switch.

